NAME
====

**wattle-test** - run the tests of a project

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle test** [_options_]

DESCRIPTION
===========

Run the tests. ***test*** runs each file ending in ``.wattle`` under ``./test``,
in a process of its own. It prints ``seed:`` and the seed. It then prints one
line for each file, with a mark, the path and the counts of tests and
assertions. It prints the output of a file that failed after its line, each
line after a border that is red when colour is on. It ends with the number of
files and tests and the files that failed. The output of a file that passed is
not printed. The exit status is 1 if a file failed or no file was run. A test
file that uses the Gum test module, ``gum/test.wattle``, reads the dynamic
bindings that **-t**, **-T** and **--seed** set. **t** is a synonym for
***test***.

OPTIONS
=======

- **-f**, **--file** _path_:
  Run only the test file whose path ends with _path_, which is relative to
  ``./test``. It can be repeated. It is not compatible with **-F**.

- **-F**, **--no-file** _path_:
  Do not run the test file whose path ends with _path_. It can be repeated. It
  is not compatible with **-f**.

- **-t**, **--test** _name_:
  Add _name_ to the dynamic binding ``:test/tests`` in each test file. It can
  be repeated. It is not compatible with **-T**.

- **-T**, **--no-test** _name_:
  Add _name_ to the dynamic binding ``:test/skips`` in each test file. It can
  be repeated. It is not compatible with **-t**.

- **--seed** _seed_:
  Use the integer _seed_ to seed the generator that shuffles the test files.
  Each test file also shuffles its tests with it, as ***test*** sets the dynamic
  binding ``:test/seed``. Without **--seed**, the seed is taken from the clock,
  so each run has a different order. The same seed gives the same order.

- **-b**, **--bail**:
  Stop after the first test file that fails.

- **-e**, **--lint-error** _level_, **-w**, **--lint-warn** _level_:
  Set the lint levels of each test file. They take the same values as for
  **wattle** ***check***.

EXAMPLES
========

Run the tests in ``./test``, skipping one file:

````
$ wattle test --no-file slow.wattle
````

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`, `wattle-check(1)`
